                    "examDate": null,
                    "question": {
                        "en": {
                            "content": "\"His face ___________ with joy when the solution of the puzzle was _______ to him.\"\n<br><br>The words that best fill the blanks in the above sentence are",
                            "options": [
                                {
                                    "identifier": "A",
                                    "content": "shone, shown"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "B",
                                    "content": "shone, shone"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "C",
                                    "content": "shown, shone"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "D",
                                    "content": "shown, shown"
                                }
                            ],
                            "correct_options": [
                                "A"
                            ],
                            "answer": null,
                            "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is <strong>Option A: shone, shown</strong>. Here's why:</p>\n\n<p>Let's analyze each word and its usage in the sentence:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Shone:</strong>  This is the past tense of the verb \"to shine,\" which means to emit light or to be bright. In the context of the sentence, \"his face shone with joy\" implies that his face lit up with happiness.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Shown:</strong> This is the past participle of the verb \"to show,\" which means to make something visible or to reveal something. In the context of the sentence, \"the solution of the puzzle was shown to him\" implies that the solution was revealed to him.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the sentence should read: \"His face <strong>shone</strong> with joy when the solution of the puzzle was <strong>shown</strong> to him.\" This accurately captures the emotional response of the person and the action of revealing the solution.</p>\n\n<p></p>"
                        }
                    },
