                    "examDate": null,
                    "question": {
                        "en": {
                            "content": "Given that $${{\\log \\,P} \\over {y - z}} = {{\\log \\,Q} \\over {z - x}} = {{\\log \\,R} \\over {x - y}} = 10$$ for $$x \\ne y \\ne z$$, what is the value of the product\nPQR?",
                            "options": [
                                {
                                    "identifier": "A",
                                    "content": "0"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "B",
                                    "content": "1"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "C",
                                    "content": "xyz"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "D",
                                    "content": "10<sup>xyz</sup>"
                                }
                            ],
                            "correct_options": [
                                "B"
                            ],
                            "answer": null,
                            "explanation": "<p>The given equation is:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\frac{{\\log \\,P}}{{y - z}} = \\frac{{\\log \\,Q}}{{z - x}} = \\frac{{\\log \\,R}}{{x - y}} = 10 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Let's denote this common value by $$k = 10$$. Therefore, we can write:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\frac{{\\log \\,P}}{{y - z}} = k \\implies \\log \\,P = k(y - z) $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\frac{{\\log \\,Q}}{{z - x}} = k \\implies \\log \\,Q = k(z - x) $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\frac{{\\log \\,R}}{{x - y}} = k \\implies \\log \\,R = k(x - y) $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Now, let's sum these three equations:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\log \\,P + \\log \\,Q + \\log \\,R = k(y - z) + k(z - x) + k(x - y) $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>The right-hand side simplifies as follows:</p>\n\n<p>$$ k(y - z + z - x + x - y) = k \\cdot 0 = 0 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Thus, we have:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\log \\,P + \\log \\,Q + \\log \\,R = 0 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Using properties of logarithms, this can be rewritten as:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ \\log (PQR) = 0 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Exponentiating both sides of the equation (with base 10), we get:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ 10^{\\log (PQR)} = 10^0 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Therefore:</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<p>$$ PQR = 1 $$</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Thus, the value of the product $$PQR$$ is $$1$$. The correct option is:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Option B: 1</strong></p>"
                        }
                    },
